This photograph of Jason and his mother

00:36:57.299 --> 00:37:00.879
was taken in Paris a day before he met you.

00:37:06.339 --> 00:37:07.179
No, that can't be.

00:37:07.980 --> 00:37:09.139
His mom was in the Hamptons.

00:37:09.139 --> 00:37:11.219
Look, Lana, I'm not going to be so presumptuous

00:37:11.219 --> 00:37:12.980
as to judge Jason's integrity.

00:37:14.059 --> 00:37:15.359
But I'll lay out a few facts.

00:37:17.179 --> 00:37:18.639
Genevieve Teague has been researching,

00:37:18.639 --> 00:37:20.879
the Countess since before Jason was born.

00:37:22.400 --> 00:37:25.259
He grew up in a house full of ancient artifacts

00:37:25.259 --> 00:37:28.639
and reams of research material about Margaret Isabel Thoreau.

00:37:28.639 --> 00:37:30.400
He never told me that.

00:37:30.400 --> 00:37:32.639
Contrary to what you may think,

00:37:32.639 --> 00:37:35.259
Jason's been aware of the Countess since he was a child.

00:37:40.139 --> 00:37:40.639
No.

00:37:41.759 --> 00:37:42.759
No, I don't believe that.

00:37:43.879 --> 00:37:45.259
You have to ask yourself, Lana.

00:37:47.759 --> 00:37:48.259
How well do you really know Jason?

00:37:48.260 --> 00:37:50.260
Do you really know Jason Teague?

00:37:50.260 --> 00:37:52.260
.

00:38:02.260 --> 00:38:03.260
Knock, knock.

00:38:03.760 --> 00:38:05.760
You should think about putting up a door or something.

00:38:05.760 --> 00:38:08.260
I don't know, maybe it's a city thing, but where I come from,

00:38:08.260 --> 00:38:09.760
we like to have a little privacy.

00:38:11.260 --> 00:38:13.500
Lois, who would have thought I'd be relieved to hear your voice?

00:38:14.260 --> 00:38:17.260
Look, Clark, I don't know how you did it, but...

00:38:18.260 --> 00:38:21.260
if it weren't for you, I'd be at the bottom of the Mississippi right about now.

00:38:22.260 --> 00:38:23.260
Thanks.

00:38:23.760 --> 00:38:24.760
I'm just glad you're okay.

00:38:25.260 --> 00:38:26.760
And going back to school.

00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:29.260
That's not entirely true.

00:38:29.260 --> 00:38:31.760
I kind of got punted out of the university.

00:38:32.760 --> 00:38:34.760
I thought you were cleared of all charges.

00:38:35.260 --> 00:38:36.260
Oh, I was, but...

00:38:36.760 --> 00:38:40.260
see, the thing is, I'm still busted for the booze, and, well...

00:38:40.760 --> 00:38:44.260
that wasn't the first time I've been invited to the disciplinary board's kangaroo court.

00:38:44.260 --> 00:38:46.260
Well, why am I not surprised?

00:38:46.260 --> 00:38:48.260
You heading back to the barracks?

00:38:48.260 --> 00:38:49.260
Not an option.

00:38:49.260 --> 00:38:52.260
My dad's trying out the tough love approach with an emphasis on tough.

00:38:52.760 --> 00:38:54.760
So what are you gonna do? You gonna go stay with Chloe?

00:38:55.760 --> 00:38:57.260
They've got a tiny one-bedroom apartment.

00:38:57.260 --> 00:38:58.260
I can't do that to them.

00:38:58.760 --> 00:39:01.260
It's fine, really. I'm just gonna check into a motel, and...

00:39:01.760 --> 00:39:04.260
when the money runs out, I can always sleep in my car.

00:39:04.260 --> 00:39:07.260
Backseat's not too bad if you bend your knees and avoid the drive train, and...

00:39:07.260 --> 00:39:07.760
Lois...

00:39:07.760 --> 00:39:11.760
And then, you know, if I have to sell my car for food, that's okay, too.

00:39:11.760 --> 00:39:15.760
I've always dreamed of being a hobo, riding the rails, cooking beans over roadside fires.

00:39:16.260 --> 00:39:21.760
If you want, I guess you could stay with us.

00:39:21.760 --> 00:39:23.760
You're a lifesaver. God, am I in need of a hot shower.

00:39:25.760 --> 00:39:28.760
Don't worry, Smallville. I'll try to keep it under a half hour.

00:39:33.760 --> 00:39:34.760
What just happened?

00:39:46.260 --> 00:39:47.760
Hey!

00:39:47.760 --> 00:39:51.760
Looks like you've got a carpool buddy for weekenders back to Smallville.

00:39:51.760 --> 00:39:52.760
You got in and met you?

00:39:52.760 --> 00:39:55.760
The financial aid guy said that it's pretty much a lock.

00:39:55.760 --> 00:39:57.760
Can you believe it? Now I don't actually have to rob banks.

00:39:57.760 --> 00:39:59.760
Oh, Chloe, congratulations. You deserve it.

00:39:59.760 --> 00:40:00.760
Thank you.

00:40:00.760 --> 00:40:03.760
You just have to promise me one thing, that once you're everybody's All-American,

00:40:03.760 --> 00:40:06.760
you will still remember your old high school buddy.

00:40:06.760 --> 00:40:08.760
I mean, you'll still say hi to me on campus and stuff.

00:40:08.760 --> 00:40:10.760
Yeah, um, well, I'm not going to Met You.

00:40:10.760 --> 00:40:11.760
What?

00:40:12.760 --> 00:40:13.760
I'm not going to Met You.

00:40:13.760 --> 00:40:14.760
What?

00:40:14.760 --> 00:40:15.760
I'm not going to Met You.

00:40:16.260 --> 00:40:17.260
What happened?

00:40:17.260 --> 00:40:20.260
Did another school swoop down and give you the keys to the kingdom?

00:40:20.260 --> 00:40:23.260
I'm not playing football anymore. I turned down my scholarship.

00:40:25.260 --> 00:40:26.760
Let me get this straight.

00:40:26.760 --> 00:40:30.260
You were offered a full ride with chrome wheels to play the game that you love,

00:40:30.260 --> 00:40:32.760
and you said thanks but no thanks.

00:40:34.760 --> 00:40:37.260
I don't know. I'm just not sure that football is my calling.

00:40:43.760 --> 00:40:45.260
I'm proud of you, Clark.

00:40:46.260 --> 00:40:50.260
You're proud of me. Why?

00:40:52.260 --> 00:40:58.260
I just have a feeling that you're destined to do a lot more in this world than just score touchdowns.

00:40:58.260 --> 00:41:01.260
Chloe, you've been saying a lot of weird things to me lately.

00:41:02.260 --> 00:41:04.260
What makes you think I'm destined to do anything?

00:41:07.260 --> 00:41:08.260
Just a hunch.

00:41:17.260 --> 00:41:18.260
Don't bought any of these.

00:41:23.260 --> 00:41:24.260
I miss you.

00:41:32.260 --> 00:41:39.220
Sorry I lost the

00:41:39.220 --> 00:41:39.920
microphone.

00:41:39.920 --> 00:41:41.260
Sorry I lost the information.

00:41:41.260 --> 00:41:42.260
Well, sorry.

00:41:42.260 --> 00:41:43.260
I missed the video.

00:41:43.260 --> 00:41:44.020
Sorry.

00:41:44.020 --> 00:41:45.020
We have to wrap up.

00:41:45.020 --> 00:41:46.260
How were you playing?

00:41:46.260 --> 00:41:48.940
I'm fading away

00:41:48.940 --> 00:41:51.400
I'm sick of this life

00:41:51.400 --> 00:41:54.120
I just wanna scream

00:41:54.120 --> 00:41:59.140
How could this happen to me?

